<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 80,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 of barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 80,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 of barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 40,000 tonnes of Canadian barley at its weekly tender, all for December shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results are as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000	  Dark northern spring     5,000</p>
<p>				  Hard red winter</p>
<p>				   (11.5 percent protein) 15,000</p>
<p> Canada     40,000	  Western red spring	40,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000	  Standard white	    20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> Canada     40,000	    Feed			27,000</p>
<p>				    Beer			10,000</p>
<p>				    Foods			3,000</p>
</text>
